{"title":"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that, for any fixed integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/61089b627cfcf55363f173acdd6853f85399ca9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,n \\geq 1,\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> the sequence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9bc822f0ae15f00eebdb0827fd4654386f4aef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2, \\; 2^2, \\; 2^{2^2}, \\; 2^{2^{2^2}}, \\ldots  \\pmod{n}\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"25\" />\nis eventually constant. \n</p><p>[The tower of exponents is defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/76891b294cadb92f22a0c60c22b215db68611812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 2, \\; a_{i+1} = 2^{a_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />. Also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c794b9b3813b4c1554b7c8b072b3713deecf4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\pmod{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> means the remainder which results from dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/98914ece9b176083e8b450c1f9187801ec121dbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,a_i\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86a23f1413ce0d3dea3b3ee190efed535fa170e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\,n$\" width=\"13\" height=\"8\" />.]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the problem statement is false for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.  Then there is a least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, which we call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, for which the statement is false.\n</p><p>Since all integers are equivalent mod 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc9156513ccb854120a8ff758f331f4dbd76c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Note that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd96f69027f6673f05407426f97e6249c0d6b034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^0, 2^1, 2^2, \\dotsc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> eventually becomes cyclic mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the period of this cycle.  Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> nonzero residues mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c35584c7550dd80a6557442f0702dc4ee4bd54ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k\\le b-1 &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />.  Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698c31481558552d1d3d0d9de46bdec50a637238.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2, 2^2, 2^{2^2}, 2^{2^{2^2}}, \\dotsc\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"25\" />\ndoes not become constant mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, it follows the sequence of exponents of these terms, i.e., the sequence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a7137c3aa003df4d4eb7373bb2b08512ec454f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1, 2, 2^2, 2^{2^{2}}, \\dotsc\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"22\" />\ndoes not become constant mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  Then the problem statement is false for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fbf6b1b2bc81af471428fe2dc93cf475d6cd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=k$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01f54e26adad951ea5b0e14b8f6995b45b13fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, this is a contradiction.  Therefore the problem statement is true.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Note that we may replace 2 with any other positive integer, and both the problem and this solution remain valid.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We’ll prove by strong induction that for every natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56551a1cd4be3a5d996736e858917416035f3c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> is eventually constant. Since every term of the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b67543d64a502eea3ba04934ca4a11776777c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\mathrm{\\ mod\\ } 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, the claim is true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Assuming that it’s true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f94de39ff4de8f6bcddb5b487fa1b3b51ddccae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, \\ldots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, we’ll now show that it’s true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> as well.\n</p><p>Suppose first that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is odd. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb53c3e2e200f6d50ea949af642b3aed16a3466c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(n + 1) &lt; n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />, by our inductive hypothesis there exists an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a8fc9615a8899a0bc3d8c9fd72e0868f46eaa7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_m = a_{m + 1} = a_{m + 2} = \\cdots \\pmod{\\varphi(n + 1)}.\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is coprime to powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it follows by Euler’s Totient theorem that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d5bc444f4435e5345630f15e03975f3ec6625f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{a_m} = 2^{a_{m + 1}} = 2^{a_{m + 2}} = \\cdots \\pmod{n + 1},\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>or equivalently\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcb3a2f8194a8054f5b4d13da1db9fa640cd247.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{m + 1} = a_{m + 2} = a_{m + 3} = \\cdots \\pmod{n + 1},\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>which is what we wanted to show.\n</p><p>Now suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is even. Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f414c941179fb61e1c21fcc0a0bc1f617f3eb4b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1 = 2^{k} \\cdot s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238cd2e6db4af231737a34e9d9ea5105261ddd1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq s &lt; n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> is odd. The series must eventually be constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076e96c23936cc95e27b81be921b0441fb042dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{mod\\ } 2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8af5d3f8bd067613b48837824fbc55f1e1f398d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m = 0 \\textrm{\\ mod\\ } {2^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> for large enough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. And by our inductive hypothesis, the series must also eventually be constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19f3c633a26e76f2a0c90040c29244416213213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{mod\\ } s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />. So for large enough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/03898e3f56d9581369a2fc5895c6f85696626f6f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_m = a_{m + 1} = a_{m + 2} = \\cdots \\pmod{2^k},\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7f670a24b6d5f7031fe41b81f724fe578603ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_m = a_{m + 1} = a_{m + 2} = \\cdots \\pmod{s}.\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are coprime, these equations are also true modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef33c2e2a92fa284ddbf6f9bb91b833cce2e040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k \\cdot s = n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" />. So\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac49786a9d014a4897c0253b8b19d021e16ae8fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_m = a_{m + 1} = a_{m + 2} = \\cdots \\pmod{n + 1},\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>which completes the proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO\" title=\"1991 USAMO\">1991 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1991 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=113561#113561\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=110644#110644\">Discussion of generalization</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017182916\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 305/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9439/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.615      1 -total\n 58.82%    7.420      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 38.60%    4.870      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6273:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017182916 and revision id 281373. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}